Vikram and Betal: The Clever Girl

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began another story.

“Once there was a poor girl who was very clever,” said Betal. “She lived with her mother and helped her in all her work.”

One day, a rich man lost his ring and accused the girl of stealing it.

The girl said, “I did not take your ring.”

The case was taken to the king.

The king asked, “How can we find the truth?”

The clever girl said, “Give everyone a stick and say it will grow if they are guilty.”

Everyone agreed.

The next day, all the sticks were the same size.

The girl said, “If anyone was guilty, they would have cut their stick out of fear.”

The king realized that the rich man was lying.

The girl was proven innocent.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, who was truly clever?”

Vikram replied, “The girl was clever because she used her intelligence to prove the truth.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Intelligence helps reveal the truth.
